+ `No tools. Read-only discussion of these supplied synthetic roofing worksheet inputs: developed rectangle 8 m wide by 9.8 m run; effective cover 0.8 m; identical ordered sheet lengths 5 m; end lap 0.2 m. Explain the first-course-full rule, the columns/courses/sheets and ordered linear metres. Explain course-count boundaries at a run of 5 m, just above 5 m, 9.8 m and just above 9.8 m. Effective cover already includes side lap. Do not deduct it twice. Include a concise Developer review of your answer. Use at most 220 words. No project reads/changes or fresh execution claims; retain draft and quote-ineligible limits.`,
+ `No tools. Read-only discussion of supplied synthetic QS export evidence. Two unverified m2 items A=0.10 assigned to child Walls, B=0.20 unassigned; one sample lm item C=3 assigned to Walls; an inferred m2 item D=4 assigned directly to Building. Building is parent of Walls. Explain whole versus filtered totals, why inclusive parent and child totals must not be summed, and the difference between a flat item-only CSV and a hierarchical CSV labelled SUMMARY_NODE versus LEAF_ITEM. State what should be summed in each, keep units and evidence classes separate, and explain the apostrophe protecting a formula-like item name =1+1. Include concise Developer review. At most 220 words. These are supplied observations, not a fresh app inspection or export; source references are unavailable, draft classification and verifiedQuoteEligible=false.`
